<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Perfils</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Perfils: Generate topographic profiles</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>This module generates topographic profiles for a specific itinerary (represented by an ARC file with the restrictions that are specified below)  using a Digital Elevation Model (DEM).</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Generate topographic profiles"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This module generates topographic profiles for a specific itinerary (represented by an ARC file with the restrictions that are specified below)  using a Digital Elevation Model (DEM)."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Creating a topographic profile.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MDE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Raster file of DEM</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Input raster file of the Digital Elevation Model.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:MDE"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-img</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Itinerari</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Track file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Arc-structured vector with the route from which the topographic profile is determined.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Track"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ModeInterpol</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Interpolation mode</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[Interpolation mode. <ul><li>0 Closest neighbour</li><li>1 Bilineal interpolation</li><li>2 Bicubic interpolation</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:InterpolMode"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Pendent</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Slope</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[Option to display the slope of each section. <ul><li>0 Without slope</li><li>1 Slope expressed in degrees</li><li>2 Slope expressed in percent</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Slope"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Obrir</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Open</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If this parameter is active, once all the  necessary components have been created, the graphic will be viewed  in a new MiraMon session. In this case, the parameter /SAC is  added automatically in order to prevent interruptions. This means  that the options will be chosen by default.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FACTOR_H</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>H factor</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Distortion factor that allows you to dilate (values >1, usual option) or contract (values &lt;1), the dimensions of the Y axis with respect to the X axis in order to show the profile that is closest proportionally to the most common X/Y dimensions of the screen and/or the paper.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
					<DefaultValue>1</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>X_NDIV</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>X NDIV</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This fixes the number of divisions of the X axes. In the absence of this parameter, the most suitable number is calculated so that the number of divisions implies a series of spaced labels in pre-established multiples of tens, hundreds, thousands, etc.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Y_NDIV</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Y NDIV</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This fixes the number of divisions of the Y axes. In the absence of this parameter, the most suitable number is calculated so that the number of divisions implies a series of spaced labels in pre-established multiples of tens, hundreds, thousands, etc.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>X_MULT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>X Mult</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This ensures that the labels of X axes are multiples of any given desired value.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Y_MULT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Y Mult</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>This ensures that the labels of Y axes are multiples of any given desired value.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>X_OFFSET</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>X Offset</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The origin of X axes is explicitly configured. This is useful when one wishes to superimpose two histograms with different origins.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Y_OFFSET</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Y Offset</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The origin of Y axes is explicitly configured. This is useful when one wishes to superimpose two histograms with different origins.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Z_UNITATS_MDT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Z units of DEM</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>In the absence of this parameter, the heights of the topographic profile will be the units of its vertical reference system (usually meters), in such a way that if there are other units in the DEM (for example, dm), they will be transformed into the system's units (m). However, if you wish to keep the original DEM units or, more commonly, if you wish to generate a profile for any other variable (for example, temperature), the units of the Y axis of the histogram will be those of the Digital Terrain Model (DTM).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DIST_3D</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Dist 3D</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The absence of this parameter indicates that
          the distance to the origin calculated using the (X, Y) planimetric
          components is represented on the X axis of the histogram.
          Conversely, its presence determines a series of longer (or
          identical, for a flat itinerary) distances by also taking into
          account movements due to height differences. Therefore, this
          distance is more similar to the route taken over the surface of the
          terrain and is not useful for profiles on temperature maps,
          etc.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#float">float</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>CONSERVAR_COTA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Conserve height</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If the file is a 3D arcs file, it will use preferentially these data to do the profile. If there are points with no 3D information or the file is a 2D arcs file, it will use the DEM in those points.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DESC</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Add description to axes</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Add description to axes with units. On the X axis, it indicates Distance (or Distance over the terrain if /DIST_3D has been specified). On the Y axis, it indicates the descriptor of the Digital Terrain Model layer.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DESC_Y</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Add custom description to Y axis</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Add description for the Y axis of the generated graph. On the X axis, it indicates Distance (or Distance over the terrain if /DIST_3D has been specified).</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>DIR_GRAFICS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Output folder</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>A directory where all the files that make up the graphic are created. If this directory is not chosen, the map and its components will be created in the temporary directory and if the parameter /OBRIR is selected, all the components of the histogram will be erased when the user closes the corresponding MiraMon session.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:GraphicFolder"/>
				<LiteralOutput>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#anyURI">anyURI</ows:DataType>
				</LiteralOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>